stanceDates":"16 October-16 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"830002AGPNHQCJGMVBQMVNGPDNHGDQVTB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-16T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-16T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-16T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-16T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"720501","attribute_Certificate":"N/A","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"N/A","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"N/A","attribute_EventType":"Theatre","attribute_Genre":"Music","attribute_ScreenNumber":"1","attribute_SendToDCM":"No","attribute_Sitename":"Gala","attribute_Genre1":"","attribute_Genre2":"","attribute_Genre3":"","attribute_Director":"","attribute_Cast":"","attribute_PaymentGateway":"","attribute_PaymentID":""},{"description":"Elysium Theatre Company \r\n\r\nLike many of Ibsen's plays, Ghosts is a scathing commentary on 19th-century morality. Because of its subject matter, which includes religion, venereal disease, incest, and euthanasia,[3] it immediately generated strong controversy and adverse criticism.\r\n\r\nSince then, the play has come to be considered a \"great play\"[4] that historically holds a position of \"immense importance\".[5] Theater critic Maurice Valency wrote in 1963, \"From the standpoint of modern tragedy Ghosts strikes off in a new direction.... Regular tragedy dealt mainly with the unhappy consequences of breaking the moral code. Ghosts, on the contrary, deals with the consequences of not breaking it.\"[6]","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ghosts (BATH)","instanceDates":"10 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"867002ATQRNQBGTVQQDKKQRHSLNJQRDHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-10T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-10T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-10T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-10T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"720501","attribute_Certificate":"N/A","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"XX","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"N/A","attribute_EventType":"Theatre","attribute_Genre":"Theatre","attribute_ScreenNumber":"1","attribute_SendToDCM":"No","attribute_Sitename":"BATH","attribute_Genre1":"","attribute_Genre2":"","attribute_Genre3":"","attribute_Director":"","attribute_Cast":"","attribute_PaymentGateway":"","attribute_PaymentID":""},{"description":"Elysium Theatre Company \r\n\r\nLike many of Ibsen's plays, Ghosts is a scathing commentary on 19th-century morality. Because of its subject matter, which includes religion, venereal disease, incest, and euthanasia,[3] it immediately generated strong controversy and adverse criticism.\r\n\r\nSince then, the play has come to be considered a \"great play\"[4] that historically holds a position of \"immense importance\".[5] Theater critic Maurice Valency wrote in 1963, \"From the standpoint of modern tragedy Ghosts strikes off in a new direction.... Regular tragedy dealt mainly with the unhappy consequences of breaking the moral code. Ghosts, on the contrary, deals with the consequences of not breaking it.\"[6]","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ghosts (Empire)","instanceDates":"24 February-24 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"867202ASGSBPLBGVRHLBHDMRHGVTKSQPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-24T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-24T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-24T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-24T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"720501","attribute_Certificate":"N/A","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"XX","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"N/A","attribute_EventType":"Theatre","attribute_Genre":"Theatre","attribute_ScreenNumber":"1","attribute_SendToDCM":"No","attribute_Sitename":"Empire","attribute_Genre1":"","attribute_Genre2":"","attribute_Genre3":"","attribute_Director":"","attribute_Cast":"","attribute_PaymentGateway":"","attribute_PaymentID":""},{"description":"IANT, the 5-star critically acclaimed play starring John Lithgow (Killers of the Flower Moon, The\r\nCrown) as Roald Dahl, comes to the big screen. Winner of 3 Olivier Awards® including Best Play and a\r\nTony Award® for Best Actor in a Play (John Lithgow), the production was filmed live in London’s\r\nWest End ahead of its sold-out Broadway run. The stellar cast includes Aya Cash (The Boys, The\r\nFranchise, You’re the Worst), Elliot Levey (Cold War, Patriots, Good) and Rachael Stirling (The Divine\r\nMrs S).\r\nA world-famous children’s author under threat. A battle of wills in the wake of scandal. And one\r\nchance to make amends.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"GIANT - The Play (15) (Gala)","instanceDates":"19 November-26 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"837002ABSQBKCQSLTHJBNNGTHMNKRPDGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-19T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-19T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-26T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-26T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"720501","attribute_Certificate":"15","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"515213","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"50110","attribute_EventType":"Cinema","attribute_Genre":"Screening","attribute_ScreenNumber":"1","attribute_SendToDCM":"Yes","attribute_Sitename":"Gala","attribute_Genre1":"","attribute_Genre2":"","attribute_Genre3":"","attribute_Director":"","attribute_Cast":"","attribute_PaymentGateway":"","attribute_PaymentID":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Giovanni: Unstoppable","instanceDates":"7 April-8 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"828402ALRTPNNGGQJNVKCTMLCDRGVPMQL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-07T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-07T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-08T18:30:0